    "result_text": "I added `authed_or_register` to `CTFd/utils/decorators/__init__.py`, just above `members_only`. It lets logged-in users through. It sends everyone else to `auth.register` with `next=request.full_path`, so they come back to the page after signing up. I haven't run it or added tests.\n\nI based it on the catalog's `decorators.authed_only` pattern and changed only the redirect target. JSON and event-stream requests still get a 403 instead of a redirect, as in `authed_only`.\n\nThe pattern check reports no high or medium deviations. The one low-severity note is the changed literal (`auth.login` → `auth.register`), which is what you asked for, so it needs no approval.\n\nUsage: `@authed_or_register` on a view, the same way as `@authed_only`."
